 campus landmark helps anchor the east side of Main Campus.","evidence_claim":"CU Boulder’s visitor information identifies sporting and athletics events as campus activities, and the official campus map labels Folsom Field.","source_url":"https://www.colorado.edu/visit-campus","source_title":"Visit Campus","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Viewing the exterior is a self-guided campus walk; event entry and ticketing depend on the specific event.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"varsity-lake","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Varsity Lake","title":"Pause beside Varsity Lake","subtitle":"Saturday midday · East edge of Main Campus","notes":"Use the campus map to find Varsity Lake, then take a short outdoor break before continuing toward the recreation and stadium area.","short_summary":"A named campus water feature provides a clear waypoint on a self-guided walk.","evidence_claim":"The official CU Boulder campus map labels Varsity Lake on Main Campus near Folsom Field and recreation facilities.","source_url":"https://catalog.colorado.edu/about-cu-boulder/campus-map/campus-map.pdf","source_title":"CU Boulder Campus Map","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2026-06-13","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use the current interactive campus map for routing and any access updates.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"pearl-street-mall","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Pearl Street Mall","title":"Walk the Pearl Street Mall without an agenda","subtitle":"Saturday afternoon · Downtown Boulder","notes":"Take a slow pass through the pedestrian mall, notice public art and storefronts, and pick one landmark to revisit with friends another weekend.","short_summary":"Downtown Boulder’s pedestrian center offers an easy off-campus orientation walk.","evidence_claim":"Downtown Boulder Partnership describes the Pearl Street Mall as a downtown gathering place with shopping, dining, services, and special events.","source_url":"https://boulderdowntown.com/","source_title":"Downtown Boulder Partnership","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Individual storefront hours vary by season; the downtown FAQ directs visitors to check businesses individually.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"boulder-alley-gallery","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Boulder Alley Gallery","title":"Look for art in the Boulder Alley Gallery","subtitle":"Saturday afternoon · Downtown Boulder","notes":"Turn the Pearl Street visit into a short art walk. Find several painted alley doors, take a photo, and keep moving through the public downtown district.","short_summary":"A continuing outdoor art program offers a specific visual scavenger-hunt stop.","evidence_claim":"Downtown Boulder Community Initiatives describes the Boulder Alley Gallery as an outdoor artist gallery that repurposes alley and back-of-building doors.","source_url":"https://boulderdowntown.com/events/submissions","source_title":"Artist, Band & Parade Submission","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The program is in the downtown district; consult the organizer’s Alley Gallery map before setting out.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"chautauqua-trailhead","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Chautauqua Trailhead","title":"Close with a daylight Chautauqua walk","subtitle":"Sunday morning · 900 Baseline Rd.","notes":"Choose the Chautauqua Trail for a short out-and-back, bring water, and read the interpretive signs. Check trail status and conditions immediately before leaving.","short_summary":"A mapped, easy-to-medium trail gives a first weekend a careful outdoor finish.","evidence_claim":"The City of Boulder lists Chautauqua Trail as a 1.2-mile out-and-back route through Chautauqua Meadow and advises visitors to pack extra water.","source_url":"https://bouldercolorado.gov/trail/chautauqua","source_title":"Chautauqua Trail","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The trailhead is listed as open daily 5 a.m.–11 p.m.; the city lists no trailhead fee, but notes summer parking fees may apply.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":["The CU Museum of Natural History was excluded because its official FAQ says it is closed until fall 2026."]}],"warnings":[]}
